            <ArticleTitle>Osteochondral fractures of the knee in skeletally immature patients: short term results of operative fixation using Omnitech screws.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>762-767</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Osteochondral fractures in skeletally immature patients are rare. A retrospective case series is reported looking at the use of Omnitech compression screws for these injuries.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">Nine patients with a mean age of 14 were included in the study with a mean follow up of 26 months.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The average KOOS, IKDC and Tegner Lysholm Scores were 86.7, 90.34 and 96.1 respectively.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The use of Omnitech screws in the acute setting for skeletally immature patients shows excellent short-term outcomes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
